markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Internet Access Advocacy Campaign Project Overview

#### This project-based lesson guides students in developing an advocacy campaign addressing digital equity, the digital divide, and net neutrality. Students explore real-world challenges, analyze case studies, and propose actionable solutions using AI-driven technology and policy recommendations. Through research, collaboration, and peer feedback, students refine their message and create a compelling advocacy campaign.

<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #B7E0E5; display: inline-block;"><i class="fa-solid fa-user-graduate"></i> Career Journeys
</p>

<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold;">In this project, students will:</h4>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Explain the role of hardware and infrastructure in ensuring the Internet is reliable and scalable.
</li> <br>
    <li>Analyze the societal and ethical impacts of the digital divide and net neutrality.
</li><br>
        <li>Propose actionable solutions to improve Internet access, including the role of AI-driven technologies.
</li><br>
<li>Develop a persuasive and well-supported advocacy campaign targeting a specific audience.
</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <img src="https://images.code.org/4e1b6412c687590c048f087cef0675e6-image-1741789708762.png" 
         alt="Icon of clipboard and pen" 
         style="border-radius: 10px; width: 300px; height: auto;">
  </div>
</div>

## Project Requirements


<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">🎧 Clarity & Focus
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### The campaign has a clear, well-defined focus that directly addresses a key issue related to the digital divide or net neutrality.


</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">💭 Persuasive Argument</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### The campaign effectively persuades the audience using strong reasoning, appeals to emotion or logic, and a clear call to action.



</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">✏️ Use of Evidence</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### The campaign includes well-researched evidence, statistics, or real-world examples that strongly support the argument.



</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">🧠 Technical Understanding
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### Clearly and thoroughly explains technical infrastructure (routers, switches, servers, etc) in terms of scalability and reliability. 
- #### Addresses challenges like high traffic or rural access with detailed and feasible solutions.


</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">✅ Feasibility & Actionability
</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px;">
    <p>


- #### The campaign presents a realistic, actionable solution that could be implemented.

</p></div>
</details>

---

## Project Calendar
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin-top: 15px;">

<div style="background: #fff; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 3px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); border: 2px solid #5a2ca0; font-size: 18px">
	<p style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px">
    	Day 1
    </p>
    
    <p style="font-size: 14px">
	In order to start developing an advocacy campaign, students explore challenges in Internet access and identify key issues/affected communities using case studies and real-world examples. <br><br> Students form teams and take on roles including: manager, summarizer, recorder, and time keeper.
    </p>
    
</div>

<div style="background: #fff; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 3px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); border: 2px solid #5a2ca0; font-size: 18px">
	<p style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px">
    	Day 2
    </p>
    
    <p style="font-size: 14px">
	Students clarify their campaign’s focus, audience, and key message. <br><br>Students develop a persuasive pitch that highlights the issue, solutions, and supporting evidence.
    </p>
    
</div>

<div style="background: #fff; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 3px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); border: 2px solid #5a2ca0; font-size: 18px">
	<p style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px">
    	Day 3
    </p>
    
    <p style="font-size: 14px">
	Students polish and refine their campaign, incorporating final revisions based on peer feedback and reflection.
    <br><br> Students present their advocacy campaign and engage in meaningful discussion around their pitches.
    </p>
    
</div>
</div>

<br>

<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;">
    ➡️ If you have time, check out the full <a href='https://studio.code.org/s/aif4-2025/lessons/8' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Lesson Plan</a>.
</p>


## 📝 To Do

#### Before you move on take a minute to learn about barriers in Internet access.

* #### Learn more about challenges in Internet access by exploring <a href='https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/4/lessons/7/levels/1' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>data from the Pew Research Center</a>. Click continue as you read through the levels learn about Internet use over time, home broadband use by income, Internet use by age, and more. This content is covered in Lesson 7: The Internet's Hidden Barriers.

* #### Learn more communities affected by Internet access by exploring the <a href='https://docs.google.com/document/d/1yn_Z-uroLVk7Lo5-wp9BjonpRRjnnliIUmGpoRv_2Ls/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.5ychaexmv4p8' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Persona Fact Sheets</a> from Day 1 of the Internet Access Advocacy Campaign Project. You can also interact with each of these personas using an <a href='https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/courses/artificial-intelligence-foundations-v2-2025/units/4/lessons/7/levels/6' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>AI Chatbot</a> from Lesson 7: The Internet's Hidden Barriers.

<br>

